<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abba Bagibo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 1825–1861</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abba Bagibo was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/limmu">Limmu</a>-Ennarea, the leading <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oromo">Oromo</a> monarchy of the Gibe region in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>, in the first half of the 19th century. Under him the kingdom reached its height as a market for gold, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a>, civet and slaves, with trade links to Gojjam and the coast. He married into neighbouring royal houses and welcomed Muslim traders, but his realm declined after his death.</p></div>
